        },
        "text_e9yarP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-lg",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Be honest about your situation. Does this describe you?</p><ul><li>Room under 200 sq ft – Blueair's small room collection offers <a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/shop-all/small\">dedicated purifiers </a>engineered for tight spaces</li><li>Mild allergies only – Occasional dust or light pet dander, not persistent symptoms</li><li>Cooling is priority – Summer comfort matters more than intensive air cleaning</li><li>Want simplicity – One device, one outlet</li><li>Budget constraints – Cost matters more than performance</li></ul><p>If all apply, a combo might work. If not, keep reading.</p><h2>When You Should Skip the Air Purifier Fan Combo</h2><p>Health concerns come first. Serious allergies, asthma, or respiratory sensitivities require maximum air purification. Combos won't deliver what you need. Learn what<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/asthma\"> asthma-friendly </a>purifiers require to understand the performance gap.</p><p>Room size matters. Most combos perform best under 300 sq ft. Larger rooms need the higher CADR only dedicated purifiers provide.</p><p>Special filtration needs. Homes with pets need both HEPA and carbon filters. Discover <a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/pet-odor-solutions-nontoxic-sustainable-air-care-that-s-safe-for-pets-and-your-home\">pet-specific odor solutions</a> that dedicated purifiers deliver.</p><p>Cost per performance. Premium combos ($700+) deliver weaker cleaning than dedicated purifiers costing one-third the price.</p><p>Skip the combo if you: suffer moderate-to-severe allergies, live in rooms over 300 sq ft, have pets, or want optimal air quality improvement.</p><h2>Why Separate Devices Outperform Combos</h2><p>Running separate devices gives you complete control. Your purifier operates centrally for optimal circulation. Your fan handles cooling independently. Each device peaks at its primary function.</p><p>Fans don't interfere with purifier performance; they actually help circulate purified air faster, creating more even air quality distribution.</p><p>Using both together is completely safe and genuinely enhances comfort without compromising air quality.</p><h2>Why Blueair Purifiers Beat Combo Units</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
