            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Blueair uses mechanical and electrostatic filtration, not just mechanical like most competitors. This combination captures particles more efficiently, delivering cleaner air with less energy.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/blue-pure-511i-max?srsltid=AfmBOoou9ohVqcd4KEu3Kfq_LZw3Dr0tk5pLG9_drYYMG3Ke6-QUvmnY\">Our 511i model,</a> engineered for medium rooms, captures particles effectively while staying quiet and efficient, something combos struggle to balance.</p><p>Explore how Blueair's performance compares to understand <a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-performance\">why dedicated purifiers </a>deliver measurable health benefits combos can't match.</p><h2>Air Purifier Fan Combo Cost Analysis</h2><p>Combos cost $150-300 initially. Separate devices cost $250-400. Upfront, combo wins.</p><p>Long-term tells a different story. Proprietary combo filters cost more per replacement than standard filters. Over five years, this gap matters. Blueair's subscription option saves <a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/subscribe\">15% with automatic delivery</a>.</p><p>Dedicated purifiers outlast combos and often use less total energy. Total ownership cost purchase plus filters plus electricity usually favors dedicated purifiers for families keeping them 3+ years.</p><h2>Key Features to Look For in an Air Purifier Combo</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_G8mhBp": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
