        "text_awpdUe": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-0",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-0",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>True HEPA filtration. \"HEPA-type\" means inferior filters. Genuine HEPA captures 99.97% at 0.3 microns. Blueair's mechanical and electrostatic approach captures down to 0.1 microns.</p><p>CADR ratings. This objective metric measures how much clean air a device produces. Use Blueair's room-sizing guide to match CADR to your space.</p><p>Noise levels. Look for under 50 dB on medium settings. Premium models operate at 25-30 dB.</p><p>Smart features. Wi-Fi, air quality sensors, and auto mode add convenience but aren't essential.</p><h3>Health Impact: What Matters</h3><p>Americans spend 90% of time indoors, where air quality significantly affects health.</p><p>Dedicated purifiers with higher CADR ratings remove allergens, mold, bacteria, and viruses more effectively. For families with young children or elderly members, superior cleaning provides measurable benefits.</p><p>If anyone has allergies or asthma, the difference between adequate and excellent cleaning directly impacts symptoms and sleep quality.</p><h2>Get Your Air Purifiers Today</h2><p>Combo units do both jobs adequately but neither exceptionally.</p><p>If space and budget are tight with only mild air quality concerns, they work. But if you have allergies, asthma, pets, or larger rooms, dedicated purifiers deliver measurable health improvement combos can't match.</p><p>Explore<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifiers\"> Blueair purifiers </a>for various room sizes engineered specifically for your family's needs. Your home should be where your air quality is best, not a compromise.</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q. Can you run an air purifier and fan together?</strong></p><p>Yes, completely safe and beneficial. The fan circulates purified air faster, creating even distribution.</p><p><strong>Q. Do combos use more electricity?</strong></p><p>Most draw similar watts separately. Efficient purifiers often use less total energy. Check wattage before purchasing.</p><p><strong>Q. How often do you replace filters?</strong></p><p>Every 6-12 months typically. Proprietary combo filters may cost more. <a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifier-filters\">Browse </a>replacement options to understand the cost difference.</p><p><strong>Q. Are combos good for allergies?</strong></p><p>Help with mild-to-moderate allergies. Severe allergies or asthma need dedicated purifiers with higher CADR.</p><p><strong>Q. Best room size for combos?</strong></p><p>Under 300 sq ft. Larger spaces need dedicated purifiers with higher capacity.</p><p><strong>Q. Note on Performance Standards</strong></p><p>All performance claims refer to HEPA filtration standards and CADR ratings as measured by industry testing protocols. Results vary based on room size, air quality, and usage.</p><h3>References</h3><p>Blueair Official Resources</p><ul><li>Air purifier specifications and performance metrics</li><li>Mechanical and electrostatic filtration technology</li><li>Product sizing guides and recommendations</li></ul><p>Industry Standards</p><ul><li>AHAM CADR ratings and verification standards</li><li>EPA indoor air quality guidance</li><li>HEPA filtration standards</li></ul>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        }
